# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ECG Learn — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development, and set the same keys in your
# Vercel project for production. NEVER commit real values. See DEPLOY.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Database (libSQL / Turso) ----------------------------------------------
# RUNTIME connection used by the app (src/lib/prisma.ts, via the libSQL adapter).
#   • Local dev: leave BOTH blank → the app uses the local file ./prisma/dev.db.
#   • Production (Vercel): REQUIRED. Point at your Turso database.
#       TURSO_DATABASE_URL="libsql://<your-db>-<your-org>.turso.io"
#       TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN="<token from: turso db tokens create ...>"
# In production the app fails fast if TURSO_DATABASE_URL is not set (no silent
# fallback to a local file that doesn't exist on a serverless host).
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=""
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=""

# LOCAL ONLY. Used by the Prisma CLI (`db push` / `migrate` / `ingest`) — this is
# the SQLite file the ingestion scripts write. Not read at runtime, and NOT needed
# on Vercel (`prisma generate` runs fine without it). Set it locally only.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# --- Auth.js (NextAuth v5) ---------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED. Secret used to sign session JWTs. Generate a fresh random value:
#     npx auth secret        (writes one for you)
#   or: openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=""

# OPTIONAL. Canonical site URL. Auto-detected on Vercel, so usually leave blank.
# Set it only if sign-in callbacks resolve to the wrong host.
#   AUTH_URL="https://your-domain.com"
AUTH_URL=""
